<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- freerdp-tk's Python (python/bin/python3.13) under the hardened runtime: no entitlement.
     sign-mac.sh passes none while this dict is empty.
     - library validation: every Mach-O of the Python (libpython, _tkinter and _dbm, Tcl/Tk and
       their thread and itcl packages) is signed by our team, and library validation loads code
       "signed by Apple or signed with the same Team ID as the main executable" (Apple,
       com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation): no disable-library-validation;
     - ctypes: python-build-standalone links libffi into libpython in its trampoline-table mode
       (ffi_closure_trampoline_table_page: callbacks use ready-made trampoline pages, never
       writable and executable memory): no allow-unsigned-executable-memory, no allow-jit;
     - no DYLD_* variable is used (the start script sets PYTHONPATH only): no
       allow-dyld-environment-variables.
     The probe's signed job proves it: tkinter, Tcl's Thread and itcl packages, a ctypes
     callback, freerdp-tk and keyring under the runtime; it also tries the larger sets, to say
     which is the least that works if this one ever fails. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
